# Every folder with a SHA256SUMS file is checked byte for byte (tools/licences/generate.py and the
# loaders). Git on Windows would turn LF into CRLF in the text files there (JSON profiles, LICENSE
# files) and break the hashes, so these folders get no line-ending conversion. A new SHA256SUMS
# folder outside data/ needs its own line here.
data/** -text
crates/ym-film/tests/oracle/** -text
